# Ignore ALL wmake-generated build folders
**/linux64Gcc**/

# Ignore object files and dep files (even if outside that folder)
*.o
*.dep

# Ignore OpenFOAM wmake temporary metadata
sourceFiles
variables

# Ignore tests folder
/tests

# Ignore TODO file
/TODO.md

/auxFiles

# Ignore vscode files
.vscode


# SMOKE BEDS: track the case DEFINITIONS, ignore the run output.
#
# These were ignored wholesale as "local validation/scratch run directories",
# and that is exactly why they rotted. Being invisible to `git status` meant no
# key-rename sweep ever reached them, and by 2026-09-02 all five carried FOUR
# settings the solver had come to reject and none of them could start:
# limitVoltageRiseRate + maxVoltageRiseRate, a dangling appliedVoltage, a
# missing electronEnergyModel, and an unsplit chemistrySolver. They are the
# smoke tests -- the thing that is supposed to catch a broken build -- and they
# were themselves broken and unnoticed.
#
# The run output is genuinely scratch, and 614 MB of it, so only that is
# ignored.
#
# NOTE the time-directory patterns deliberately do NOT use `[0-9]*`, which
# matches `0.orig` and would ignore the initial-field TEMPLATES. That glob has
# already destroyed 0.orig twice here; the failure surfaces much later as
# "cannot find file .../0/ePotential", which names the wrong thing entirely.
smoke/*/0/
smoke/*/[0-9]*.[0-9]*/
smoke/*/[0-9]*e-[0-9]*/
smoke/*/logs/
smoke/*/postProcessing/
smoke/*/log.*
smoke/*/run.log
smoke/*/case.foam
smoke/*/constant/polyMesh/
smoke/*/constant/plasmaTables/
# NOT `smoke/*/constant/*/`: that would silently ignore per-region
# material files (constant/<region>/electricalProperties) if a smoke bed
# ever became multi-region -- the same invisibility that caused this mess.
smoke/*/system/*/
# build artefacts: generated from fvSolution-foam / etc/changeDictionary
smoke/*/system/fvSolution
smoke/*/system/changeDictionaryDict

# per-component build logs and local run helpers: machine-specific, and they
# churn on every build
buildlogs/
build.log
rebuild.log

# local run helpers: personal workflow, not part of the toolkit. build-all.sh
# is kept -- it is the documented, dependency-ordered build entry point.
watchdog.sh
check-run.sh
make-smoke-case.sh
rerun.sh
run-guarded.sh
run-long.sh

# GENERATED SOLUTION DICTIONARIES in our own tutorials.
#
# Allrun does `cp system/fvSolution-foam system/fvSolution` (or -petsc,
# selected by `matrixSolver`) and `cp etc/changeDictionary.<region>
# system/changeDictionaryDict`. Both destinations are BUILD ARTEFACTS: an edit
# to them is silently overwritten on the next run, and they were tracked in
# some cases and not others though every case generates them.
#
# EDIT system/fvSolution-foam AND etc/changeDictionary.* INSTEAD.
tutorials/**/system/fvSolution
tutorials/**/system/changeDictionaryDict

# EXCEPT needleDBD, whose system/fvSolution is HAND-AUTHORED and is the only
# copy: that case has no -foam/-petsc pair, because the pair exists solely to
# switch linear-solver backends and an OpenFOAM solver dictionary silently
# ignores entries it does not use -- so one `ePotential` block carries both
# and `$ePotentialSolver` picks one. A `-foam` suffix with no `-petsc` sibling
# buys nothing and costs the artefact trap above.
!tutorials/plasma/soPlasmaFoam/needleDBD/system/fvSolution

# ThirdParty/ is deliberately untouched: those fvSolution files are upstream
# case definitions, not generated by anything here.

# The extruded mesh is reproducible in <1 s from the 2-D one by
# tools/msh2Dto3D.py (see SoEEDF meshes/README.md). 14 MB is not worth tracking.
tutorials/**/*_extruded.msh
